{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794815580136,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3585648001IeBXdodoUiZRVM","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e358407c001PlBu5SmOr4lIIY","type":"tool","id":"call_be1bb2590eaa4d45bc010ab0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"wc -l .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n '1,180p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"    2291 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\n# ────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO AND CONFIRM MODES)\n# ────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO AND CONFIRM MODES)\n# ────────\nrole: Deep Review Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection across review dimensions\naction: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: autonomous\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: progressive_review_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\n# ────────\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n# ────────\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n\n# ────────\n# EXECUTION MODE\n# ────────\nexecution_mode:\n  source: \"$ARGUMENTS\"\n  values: [auto, confirm]\n  default: confirm\n  rule: \"Every step, executor branch and flag in this file runs in both modes. Under confirm, also execute every block marked applies_to: confirm at the place that carries it, and apply the mode_overrides.confirm wording. Under auto, skip every block marked applies_to: confirm and keep the autonomous wording of this file.\"\nmode_overrides:\n  confirm:\n    purpose: \"Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection and user approval gates\"\n    action: \"Run deep-review loop with user confirmation at each phase transition\"\n    workflow_execution: \"interactive\"\n    approvals: \"multi_gate\"\n    approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, show results, get approval, repeat or stop\"\n    mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Pause for user at each gate. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n    phase_loop_purpose: \"Dispatch review agent iterations with approval at each step\"\n    lock_not_acquired: \"If acquired=false, stop and present recovery choices: another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n    agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope. If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and show to user for decision.\"\n    continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Inform user.\"\n    rules_always: [pause_at_approval_gates, present_clear_options_at_each_gate]\n    rules_never: [proceed_past_approval_gate_without_user_response, auto_approve_on_behalf_of_user]\n\n# ────────\n# USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n# ────────\nuser_inputs:\n  review_target: \"[REVIEW_TARGET] - What to review. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_target_type: \"[spec-folder|skill|agent|track|files] - Target type for scope derivation. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_dimensions: \"[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability] - Dimensions to check. Default: all.\"\n  review_focus: \"[optional free text] - Operator review focus that every iteration covers in addition to its dimension. Default: empty, which leaves the prompt unchanged.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path for state files. REQUIRED.\"\n  session_id: \"[SESSION_ID] - Optional caller-supplied session id for fan-out lineages. Default: timestamp.\"\n  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime only persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive) and `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived). `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and no longer accepted — see deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n  max_iterations: 7\n  convergence_threshold: 0.10\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Stop behavior. Default: convergence. max-iterations treats convergence as telemetry until the hard iteration ceiling.\"\n  dry_run: \"[DRY_RUN] - Boolean pre-flight flag. Default: false.\"\n  lineage_timeout_hours: \"[LINEAGE_TIMEOUT_HOURS] - Optional per-lineage wall-clock ceiling in hours for fan-out runs, at most 4. Default: unset, which keeps the 4 hour ceiling.\"\n  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n\n# ────────\n# DRY-RUN CONTROL\n# ────────\ndry_run_control:\n  enabled_when: \"dry_run == true\"\n  default: false\n  modes: [auto, confirm]\n  purpose: \"Run safe setup and read-only inspection, then stop before side effects.\"\n  safe_operations:\n    - \"Resolve setup inputs and artifact roots.\"\n    - \"Read current state, strategy, focus, and convergence signals.\"\n    - \"Render the next prompt to terminal preview without writing prompt files.\"\n  forbidden_operations:\n    - \"Executor dispatch.\"\n    - \"Persistent state, queue, lock, git index, memory, or graph mutation.\"\n    - \"Reducer refresh or generated artifact writes.\"\n    - \"Child-lineage spawn.\"\n  event_policy:\n    event_name: dry_run_halt\n    sink: \"terminal JSONL preview only; never append to {state_paths.state_log}\"\n    required_fields: [type, event, mode, boundary, step, timestamp]\n    optional_fields: [run, sessionId, generation, detail]\n    default_halt_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"dry_run_halt\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"boundary\":\"{dry_run_boundary}\",\"step\":\"{step_name}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n    preview_only: \"A step or branch marked dry_run_event_policy: preview-only still runs its read and classify work. It prints the event it would append as a terminal JSONL preview line and appends nothing.\"\n  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation in a step tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit event_policy.default_halt_event with that step's name and boundary to the terminal and halt. This holds in both execution modes.\"\n  boundary_labels:\n    child_spawn: \"child-spawn\"\n    state_mutation: \"state-mutation\"\n    dispatch: \"dispatch\"\n    reducer_refresh: \"reducer-refresh\"\n\n# ────────\n# CONTEXT LOADING\n# ────────\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior review context for the target and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  retrieval:\n    mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n    note: \"File reads only. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n    ladder:\n      - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n      - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n      - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n    free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -- '{review_target}' specs .skilled\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n    exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n    ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\n# ────────\n# SKILL REFERENCE\n# ────────\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    state_format: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n    strategy: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n\n# ────────\n# AGENT CONFIGURATION\n# ────────\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-review\n  agent_file: \".skilled/agents/deep-review.md\"\n  # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n  mode: subagent\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n  mcp_servers: []\n\n# ────────\n# STATE FILE PATHS\n# ────────\n# ────────\n# CANONICAL STATE WRITE MECHANISM\n# ────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n    the ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh: the migration\n    marker, the recovery baseline, the iteration-error row and the claim-adjudication gate\n    row are canonical ledger events like every other record.\n\nstate_paths:\n  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    2291 .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\n# ────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO AND CONFIRM MODES)\n# ────────\n# DEEP REVIEW: DEEP REVIEW LOOP (AUTO AND CONFIRM MODES)\n# ────────\nrole: Deep Review Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection across review dimensions\naction: Run deep-review loop from initialization through synthesis\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: autonomous\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: progressive_review_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\n# ────────\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n# ────────\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n\n# ────────\n# EXECUTION MODE\n# ────────\nexecution_mode:\n  source: \"$ARGUMENTS\"\n  values: [auto, confirm]\n  default: confirm\n  rule: \"Every step, executor branch and flag in this file runs in both modes. Under confirm, also execute every block marked applies_to: confirm at the place that carries it, and apply the mode_overrides.confirm wording. Under auto, skip every block marked applies_to: confirm and keep the autonomous wording of this file.\"\nmode_overrides:\n  confirm:\n    purpose: \"Iterative code/spec review with convergence detection and user approval gates\"\n    action: \"Run deep-review loop with user confirmation at each phase transition\"\n    workflow_execution: \"interactive\"\n    approvals: \"multi_gate\"\n    approach: \"Dispatch focused review agent per dimension, show results, get approval, repeat or stop\"\n    mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files. Pause for user at each gate. Review target is READ-ONLY.\"\n    phase_loop_purpose: \"Dispatch review agent iterations with approval at each step\"\n    lock_not_acquired: \"If acquired=false, stop and present recovery choices: another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n    agent_dispatch_timeout: \"Retry once with reduced scope. If second timeout, mark as 'timeout' and show to user for decision.\"\n    continuity_save_failure: \"Preserve the review packet in review/ as backup. Inform user.\"\n    rules_always: [pause_at_approval_gates, present_clear_options_at_each_gate]\n    rules_never: [proceed_past_approval_gate_without_user_response, auto_approve_on_behalf_of_user]\n\n# ────────\n# USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n# ────────\nuser_inputs:\n  review_target: \"[REVIEW_TARGET] - What to review. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_target_type: \"[spec-folder|skill|agent|track|files] - Target type for scope derivation. REQUIRED.\"\n  review_dimensions: \"[all|correctness,security,traceability,maintainability] - Dimensions to check. Default: all.\"\n  review_focus: \"[optional free text] - Operator review focus that every iteration covers in addition to its dimension. Default: empty, which leaves the prompt unchanged.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path for state files. REQUIRED.\"\n  session_id: \"[SESSION_ID] - Optional caller-supplied session id for fan-out lineages. Default: timestamp.\"\n  lineage_mode: \"[auto|resume|restart] - Session lifecycle intent. Default: auto. The runtime only persists lineage events for `resume` (same sessionId, no archive) and `restart` (new sessionId, generation+1, prior review/ archived). `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and no longer accepted — see deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches.\"\n  max_iterations: 7\n  convergence_threshold: 0.10\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Stop behavior. Default: convergence. max-iterations treats convergence as telemetry until the hard iteration ceiling.\"\n  dry_run: \"[DRY_RUN] - Boolean pre-flight flag. Default: false.\"\n  lineage_timeout_hours: \"[LINEAGE_TIMEOUT_HOURS] - Optional per-lineage wall-clock ceiling in hours for fan-out runs, at most 4. Default: unset, which keeps the 4 hour ceiling.\"\n  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n\n# ────────\n# DRY-RUN CONTROL\n# ────────\ndry_run_control:\n  enabled_when: \"dry_run == true\"\n  default: false\n  modes: [auto, confirm]\n  purpose: \"Run safe setup and read-only inspection, then stop before side effects.\"\n  safe_operations:\n    - \"Resolve setup inputs and artifact roots.\"\n    - \"Read current state, strategy, focus, and convergence signals.\"\n    - \"Render the next prompt to terminal preview without writing prompt files.\"\n  forbidden_operations:\n    - \"Executor dispatch.\"\n    - \"Persistent state, queue, lock, git index, memory, or graph mutation.\"\n    - \"Reducer refresh or generated artifact writes.\"\n    - \"Child-lineage spawn.\"\n  event_policy:\n    event_name: dry_run_halt\n    sink: \"terminal JSONL preview only; never append to {state_paths.state_log}\"\n    required_fields: [type, event, mode, boundary, step, timestamp]\n    optional_fields: [run, sessionId, generation, detail]\n    default_halt_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"dry_run_halt\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"boundary\":\"{dry_run_boundary}\",\"step\":\"{step_name}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n    preview_only: \"A step or branch marked dry_run_event_policy: preview-only still runs its read and classify work. It prints the event it would append as a terminal JSONL preview line and appends nothing.\"\n  halt_hook_rule: \"Before executing any command, dispatch, edit, output, template write, append_to_jsonl, append_jsonl, log_event, mcp_tool, write, or git-index mutation in a step tagged with dry_run_boundary, emit event_policy.default_halt_event with that step's name and boundary to the terminal and halt. This holds in both execution modes.\"\n  boundary_labels:\n    child_spawn: \"child-spawn\"\n    state_mutation: \"state-mutation\"\n    dispatch: \"dispatch\"\n    reducer_refresh: \"reducer-refresh\"\n\n# ────────\n# CONTEXT LOADING\n# ────────\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior review context for the target and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  retrieval:\n    mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n    note: \"File reads only. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n    ladder:\n      - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n      - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n      - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n    free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -- '{review_target}' specs .skilled\"\n    recipe_contract: \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n    exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n    ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\n# ────────\n# SKILL REFERENCE\n# ────────\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    state_format: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n    strategy: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n\n# ────────\n# AGENT CONFIGURATION\n# ────────\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-review\n  agent_file: \".skilled/agents/deep-review.md\"\n  # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n  mode: subagent\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n  mcp_servers: []\n\n# ────────\n# STATE FILE PATHS\n# ────────\n# ────────\n# CANONICAL STATE WRITE MECHANISM\n# ────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n    the ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh: the migration\n    marker, the recovery baseline, the iteration-error row and the claim-adjudication gate\n    row are canonical ledger events like every other record.\n\nstate_paths:\n  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"wc -l .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n '1,180p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794815579720,"end":1794815580136}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794815582481,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"id":"prt_1e3586111001y06cM4WWORXowt","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e358407c001PlBu5SmOr4lIIY","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"22150c89fa1d75e54407f771d577d40f659b9aae","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":2761,"output":74,"reasoning":54,"cache":{"read":36608,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794815586278,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"id":"prt_1e3586fe6001Vj816RoH4PM1Xb","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e3586117001VI4SpfxI73AjQx","type":"step-start","snapshot":"22150c89fa1d75e54407f771d577d40f659b9aae"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794815586614,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3586fe8001BjEfH7hHzuMDcY","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e3586117001VI4SpfxI73AjQx","type":"tool","id":"call_ad0d8eda41f343e6bd183a91","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '180,330p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n  # root-local review/ and child phases keep local review/ packet dirs.\n  # Canonical root-spec write targets remain review/deep-review-config.json,\n  # review/deep-review-state.jsonl, and review/deep-review-findings-registry.json.\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  # Per-iteration structured delta stream — complement to the canonical state_log\n  # append. MUST contain at least one record with `type === \"iteration\"`; variants\n  # like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer.\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n\n# ────────\n# WORKFLOW\n# ────────\n\ngate_defaults:\n  after_gate_refresh_lock:\n    action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the operator response\"\n    command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n\nworkflow:\n\n  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n    description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n    note: \"Root specs keep review artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/review/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/review/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/review-archive/{packet}/.\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_subfolder: null\n        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n    if_absent:\n      command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'review')));\\\"\"\n      outputs:\n        - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local review owner directory\"\n        - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local review archive directory for this target\"\n\n  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n    description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n    if_absent:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n\n  step_apply_lifecycle_request:\n    description: \"Honor an explicit restart request before fan-out or normal initialization\"\n    dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n    skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n    instructions: |\n      Run this step in both execution modes, immediately after artifact resolution\n      and before fan-out, so old packet files cannot be merged with fresh lineage\n      outputs. A restart request must never fall back to resume. The explicit\n      restart flag is operator authorization to archive the resolved review packet,\n      so do not ask for a second confirmation. Rollback is to move the timestamped\n      archive back to the packet directory.\n    bind_prior_lineage:\n      action: \"Read the session id and generation of the packet that is about to be archived\"\n      command: |\n        node -e '\n          const fs = require(\"fs\");\n          const crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n          let priorSessionId = null;\n          let priorGeneration = 0;\n          try {\n            const config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1], \"utf8\"));\n            const lineage = config.lineage || config;\n            priorSessionId = typeof lineage.sessionId === \"string\" ? lineage.sessionId : null;\n            priorGeneration = Number(lineage.generation) || 0;\n          } catch (error) {\n            if (error.code !== \"ENOENT\") {\n              console.error(\"The old config cannot be read: \" + error.message);\n              process.exit(1);\n            }\n          }\n          let priorTailDigest = crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(\"\").digest(\"hex\");\n          try {\n            priorTailDigest = crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(process.argv[2])).digest(\"hex\");\n          } catch (error) {\n            if (error.code !== \"ENOENT\") throw error;\n          }\n          console.log(JSON.stringify({ priorSessionId, priorGeneration, priorTailDigest }));\n        ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n      outputs:\n        - prior_session_id: \"priorSessionId from the JSON output, null when no old config exists\"\n        - prior_generation: \"priorGeneration from the JSON output, 0 when no old config exists\"\n        - prior_tail_digest: \"priorTailDigest from the JSON output: the sha256 of the old state log bytes, or of zero bytes when no old state log exists\"\n      on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL. The old config is unreadable, so repair or archive the packet by hand.\"\n    command: |\n      if [ -e \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" ]; then\n        echo \"The archive folder {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} is already there.\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      if [ -d \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" ]; then\n        mkdir -p \"{state_paths.archive_root}\" && mv \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" || exit 1\n      fi\n      mkdir -p \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\"\n    outputs:\n      - archived_path: \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} when a prior packet existed, else null\"\n      - lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n    on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL; do not continue as resume or auto.\"\n\n  step_fanout_spawn:\n    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n    dry_run_boundary: \"child-spawn\"\n    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n    instructions: |\n      Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n      isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n      This step runs before phase_init, so pass the raw review_focus. fanout-run.cjs\n      normalizes it and hands every lineage the same single-line text. Escape any double\n      quote, backslash, dollar sign or backtick in it for the shell, and pass an empty\n      string when no focus was given.\n      A cli-opencode lineage inside this fan-out is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode\n      session with a separate lineage directory and session id; it is not the single-executor\n      self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that\n      first-level detached lineage and still blocks recursive same-kind dispatch from inside it.\n      fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n      deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n      deep-review agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n      sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n    sub_steps:\n      step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n        description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n        skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n        command: |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n  # root-local review/ and child phases keep local review/ packet dirs.\n  # Canonical root-spec write targets remain review/deep-review-config.json,\n  # review/deep-review-state.jsonl, and review/deep-review-findings-registry.json.\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  # Per-iteration structured delta stream — complement to the canonical state_log\n  # append. MUST contain at least one record with `type === \"iteration\"`; variants\n  # like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer.\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n\n# ────────\n# WORKFLOW\n# ────────\n\ngate_defaults:\n  after_gate_refresh_lock:\n    action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the operator response\"\n    command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n\nworkflow:\n\n  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n    description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n    note: \"Root specs keep review artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/review/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/review/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/review-archive/{packet}/.\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_subfolder: null\n        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n    if_absent:\n      command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'review')));\\\"\"\n      outputs:\n        - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local review owner directory\"\n        - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local review archive directory for this target\"\n\n  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n    description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n    if_absent:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n\n  step_apply_lifecycle_request:\n    description: \"Honor an explicit restart request before fan-out or normal initialization\"\n    dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n    skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n    instructions: |\n      Run this step in both execution modes, immediately after artifact resolution\n      and before fan-out, so old packet files cannot be merged with fresh lineage\n      outputs. A restart request must never fall back to resume. The explicit\n      restart flag is operator authorization to archive the resolved review packet,\n      so do not ask for a second confirmation. Rollback is to move the timestamped\n      archive back to the packet directory.\n    bind_prior_lineage:\n      action: \"Read the session id and generation of the packet that is about to be archived\"\n      command: |\n        node -e '\n          const fs = require(\"fs\");\n          const crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n          let priorSessionId = null;\n          let priorGeneration = 0;\n          try {\n            const config = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1], \"utf8\"));\n            const lineage = config.lineage || config;\n            priorSessionId = typeof lineage.sessionId === \"string\" ? lineage.sessionId : null;\n            priorGeneration = Number(lineage.generation) || 0;\n          } catch (error) {\n            if (error.code !== \"ENOENT\") {\n              console.error(\"The old config cannot be read: \" + error.message);\n              process.exit(1);\n            }\n          }\n          let priorTailDigest = crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(\"\").digest(\"hex\");\n          try {\n            priorTailDigest = crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(fs.readFileSync(process.argv[2])).digest(\"hex\");\n          } catch (error) {\n            if (error.code !== \"ENOENT\") throw error;\n          }\n          console.log(JSON.stringify({ priorSessionId, priorGeneration, priorTailDigest }));\n        ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n      outputs:\n        - prior_session_id: \"priorSessionId from the JSON output, null when no old config exists\"\n        - prior_generation: \"priorGeneration from the JSON output, 0 when no old config exists\"\n        - prior_tail_digest: \"priorTailDigest from the JSON output: the sha256 of the old state log bytes, or of zero bytes when no old state log exists\"\n      on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL. The old config is unreadable, so repair or archive the packet by hand.\"\n    command: |\n      if [ -e \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" ]; then\n        echo \"The archive folder {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} is already there.\" >&2\n        exit 1\n      fi\n      if [ -d \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" ]; then\n        mkdir -p \"{state_paths.archive_root}\" && mv \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" || exit 1\n      fi\n      mkdir -p \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\"\n    outputs:\n      - archived_path: \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} when a prior packet existed, else null\"\n      - lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n    on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL; do not continue as resume or auto.\"\n\n  step_fanout_spawn:\n    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n    dry_run_boundary: \"child-spawn\"\n    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n    instructions: |\n      Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n      isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n      This step runs before phase_init, so pass the raw review_focus. fanout-run.cjs\n      normalizes it and hands every lineage the same single-line text. Escape any double\n      quote, backslash, dollar sign or backtick in it for the shell, and pass an empty\n      string when no focus was given.\n      A cli-opencode lineage inside this fan-out is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode\n      session with a separate lineage directory and session id; it is not the single-executor\n      self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that\n      first-level detached lineage and still blocks recursive same-kind dispatch from inside it.\n      fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n      deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n      deep-review agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n      sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n    sub_steps:\n      step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n        description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n        skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n        command: |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '180,330p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794815586280,"end":1794815586614}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794815588656,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"id":"prt_1e3587930001doz6DgmWGkxAdf","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e3586117001VI4SpfxI73AjQx","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"22150c89fa1d75e54407f771d577d40f659b9aae","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":2990,"output":58,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":39296,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794815592672,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"id":"prt_1e35888e00012ZqGjzwucuottF","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e3587935001l3ug8pFqA3KjGK","type":"step-start","snapshot":"22150c89fa1d75e54407f771d577d40f659b9aae"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794815593523,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e3588981001dTPox6TEBywwmJ","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e3587935001l3ug8pFqA3KjGK","type":"tool","id":"call_4c897332a4584477bab06ae0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"step_create_state_log\\|step_reduce_state\\|phase_init:\\|phase_main_loop:\\|phase_synthesis:\\|step_init_config\\|step_init_strategy\\|step_write_review_report\\|step_terminal\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml"},"output":"349:  phase_init:\n556:          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n720:      step_create_state_log:\n1138:            when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post-iteration gate. The auto three-errors stop (reason error) reaches it through if_existing_terminal_path. The duration stop in step_check_max_duration runs it, once, before its jump to phase_synthesis. Never run it when the pivot continues the loop.\"\n1816:  phase_synthesis:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"349:  phase_init:\n556:          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n720:      step_create_state_log:\n1138:            when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post-iteration gate. The auto three-errors stop (reason error) reaches it through if_existing_terminal_path. The duration stop in step_check_max_duration runs it, once, before its jump to phase_synthesis. Never run it when the pivot continues the loop.\"\n1816:  phase_synthesis:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"step_create_state_log\\\\|step_reduce_state\\\\|phase_init:\\\\|phase_main_loop:\\\\|phase_synthesis:\\\\|step_init_config\\\\|step_init_strategy\\\\|step_write_review_report\\\\|step_terminal\\\" .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794815592833,"end":1794815593523}}}}
