{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794815957914,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e35e17c6001G35670tXGCzFb5","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e35e0ad4001n9XttYqQDIdIPb","type":"tool","id":"call_a9b0d41c8cf54a8faf743dc5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"TMPDIR\\|temp folder\\|metrics folder\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/*.md | head -20; echo =====; grep -rn \"buffer\\|listing\\|arena\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/*.md | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"The advisor suite no longer writes into the shared health-metrics folder, and the scorer prints the shape of every start beside the start rate. The split showed most counted starts are document reads alone.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:15:    packet_purpose: \"Purpose: A suite run leaves the shared metrics folder untouched, and each start rate prints the shape of its starts so a reader can apply either rule without rescoring.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:60:A suite run now leaves the shared health-metrics folder untouched, so the advisor's health readers stop counting test records as real use. The scorer also prints which shape made each start, and the split showed that most printed starts are a document read with nothing written, which the goal's fixed start rule calls a lookup.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:64:`vitest.config.ts` makes one temp folder per run with `mkdtempSync`, points `TMPDIR` at it before any worker starts and removes it when the run exits. Every test and every process a test spawns inherits it, so the advisor's metrics root, which resolves under `tmpdir()`, lands there. Before the change one full run added 6 files and 312 lines to the shared folder.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:72:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts` | Modified | Per-run temp folder, set before workers start and removed on exit |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:96:| Set `TMPDIR` in the config, not a new metrics-root option | `tmpdir()` already reads it, so every test and spawned child moves with no new knob, and the full suite passed under it |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:3:description: \"Give the advisor suite its own temp folder from vitest.config.ts, and have the scorer report and tally the shape of every start, then prove both on the shared folder and the committed 033 lines.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:29:The config makes one `mkdtempSync` folder, sets `process.env.TMPDIR` to it before Vitest starts a worker, so every `tmpdir()` call in tests and their children lands there, and removes it on process exit. `startState` gains an optional checkout folder and a `shape` field. The summary tallies the shape of each counted start, so the split sums to `started`, and prints it as `startShapes`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:62:No new file, module, option or dependency. `TMPDIR` is the variable `tmpdir()` already reads.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:65:Config load makes the folder and sets `TMPDIR`. Workers and their children inherit it, and `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT` resolves inside it. On the scorer side, `scoreLine` passes the line's `projectDir` to `startState`, the tally adds the shape of each counted start, and `tallyBlock` prints the counts.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:75:| `vitest.config.ts` | Suite config | Per-run `TMPDIR` | Shared counts unchanged after a full run |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:82:- Same-class producers: other tests that write into `tmpdir()` all move with `TMPDIR`. No other writer of the shared folder exists in the suite.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:3:description: \"The advisor suite writes health records into the operator's shared temp metrics folder, and the printed start rate hides how many starts are bare document reads. This phase gives each suite run its own temp folder and prints the shape of every start beside the rate.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:7:  - \"advisor suite shared metrics folder\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:32:| **Handoff Criteria** | A full suite run leaves the shared metrics folder unchanged, and the rescored 033 summary prints a start shape split that sums to every started count |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:50:- A suite that writes its health records under its own temp folder\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:61:`lib/metrics.ts` keeps durable health records under `join(tmpdir(), 'speckit-skill-advisor-metrics')`, and the suite runs with the operator's own temp folder, so every suite run adds test records to the folder that the health readers and the research lanes read as real use. Separately, the scorer's printed start rate counts a document read with no write as a start, while the goal's fixed arm start rule calls that a lookup, and no printed number says how many starts are of that kind.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:64:A suite run leaves the shared metrics folder untouched, and each start rate prints the shape of its starts so a reader can apply either rule without rescoring.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:73:$ TMPDIR=<fresh dir> npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:74:after TMPDIR run 729; files under per-run dir 5\n=====\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:2:title: \"Acceptance Criteria: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:5:  - \"untuned arm arena run acceptance criteria\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:19:      session_id: \"scaffold-033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:26:# Acceptance Criteria: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:40:**Packet:** 033-untuned-arm-arena-run\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:56:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given five arenas at `AC`, When every turn ends, Then each arena reads no remote and an empty status and every run line reads `restored: true` | Every arena ended at b765c7a14c5 with 0 remotes and an empty status (scratch/arenas-after.txt, the post-run check); 397 of 401 lines read restored true, the 4 fresh-skill-04 head-move lines read false (ADR-001) | Waived | ADR-001 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:2:title: \"Decision Record: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:3:description: \"Decisions taken without the operator during the untuned arm run: keeping the run when the sk-git row moved an arena's head, against the plan's rollback rule, and waiving the every-line-restored criterion for its four turns.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:5:  - \"033-untuned-arm-arena-run decisions\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:13:    recent_action: \"Recorded the decision to keep the run when one sk-git row moved an arena head\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:25:# Decision Record: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:37:| ADR-001 | Keep and score the run instead of discarding it when the four `fresh-skill-04` turns read `restored: false` (devin off run 1 twice, devin on run 1, dsh on run 1), and waive AC-001's every-line-restored clause for those four turns only. Each turn moved the arena's head with a rebase, and the runner stops on a head move before it restores. Each arena was restored by hand to `b765c7a14c5` and checked clean with no remote, and the row was not rerun past one try. The hand restore left a `main` ref in the devin and dsh arenas that a fresh arena never has (created by devin's first turn, recreated in dsh). Later turns in those two arenas ran with it, and it was deleted after the run (`scratch/arenas-after.txt`). The deciding dsh decline line ran before dsh's head move. The row stays in the scorer's counts, scored as capped on the on arm. | `fresh-skill-04` is a skill-only row whose expected top is `sk-git`, so a history operation may be the task it asks for, not an escape. Discarding 401 lines over one row the runner cannot measure would have thrown away the other 35 rows on every runtime. D1 says take the safe default without asking. | AC-001 and REQ-001 as written, plan.md section 3 invariant (every line reads `restored: true`) and plan.md section 7 rollback trigger (any line with `restored` not true) for these four turns | `scratch/devin-rebase-evidence.txt`, `scratch/dsh-head-move-evidence.txt`, `scratch/reruns.txt`, `scratch/arenas-after.txt`, goal log rows on the devin rebase |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:2:title: \"Implementation Summary: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"The untuned behaviour arm ran live on five runtimes in arenas at one commit and was scored: pooled gained 25 and lost 15 rows (p 0.0769), and dsh started a command on one decline row, so the verdict is Not shown and the B-5 trigger fired.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:5:  - \"untuned arm arena run implementation summary\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:18:      - \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:19:      - \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"The advisor suite no longer writes into the shared health-metrics folder, and the scorer prints the shape of every start beside the start rate. The split showed most counted starts are document reads alone.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:15:    packet_purpose: \"Purpose: A suite run leaves the shared metrics folder untouched, and each start rate prints the shape of its starts so a reader can apply either rule without rescoring.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:60:A suite run now leaves the shared health-metrics folder untouched, so the advisor's health readers stop counting test records as real use. The scorer also prints which shape made each start, and the split showed that most printed starts are a document read with nothing written, which the goal's fixed start rule calls a lookup.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:64:`vitest.config.ts` makes one temp folder per run with `mkdtempSync`, points `TMPDIR` at it before any worker starts and removes it when the run exits. Every test and every process a test spawns inherits it, so the advisor's metrics root, which resolves under `tmpdir()`, lands there. Before the change one full run added 6 files and 312 lines to the shared folder.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:72:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts` | Modified | Per-run temp folder, set before workers start and removed on exit |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/implementation-summary.md:96:| Set `TMPDIR` in the config, not a new metrics-root option | `tmpdir()` already reads it, so every test and spawned child moves with no new knob, and the full suite passed under it |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:3:description: \"Give the advisor suite its own temp folder from vitest.config.ts, and have the scorer report and tally the shape of every start, then prove both on the shared folder and the committed 033 lines.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:29:The config makes one `mkdtempSync` folder, sets `process.env.TMPDIR` to it before Vitest starts a worker, so every `tmpdir()` call in tests and their children lands there, and removes it on process exit. `startState` gains an optional checkout folder and a `shape` field. The summary tallies the shape of each counted start, so the split sums to `started`, and prints it as `startShapes`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:62:No new file, module, option or dependency. `TMPDIR` is the variable `tmpdir()` already reads.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:65:Config load makes the folder and sets `TMPDIR`. Workers and their children inherit it, and `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT` resolves inside it. On the scorer side, `scoreLine` passes the line's `projectDir` to `startState`, the tally adds the shape of each counted start, and `tallyBlock` prints the counts.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:75:| `vitest.config.ts` | Suite config | Per-run `TMPDIR` | Shared counts unchanged after a full run |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/plan.md:82:- Same-class producers: other tests that write into `tmpdir()` all move with `TMPDIR`. No other writer of the shared folder exists in the suite.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:3:description: \"The advisor suite writes health records into the operator's shared temp metrics folder, and the printed start rate hides how many starts are bare document reads. This phase gives each suite run its own temp folder and prints the shape of every start beside the rate.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:7:  - \"advisor suite shared metrics folder\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:32:| **Handoff Criteria** | A full suite run leaves the shared metrics folder unchanged, and the rescored 033 summary prints a start shape split that sums to every started count |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:50:- A suite that writes its health records under its own temp folder\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:61:`lib/metrics.ts` keeps durable health records under `join(tmpdir(), 'speckit-skill-advisor-metrics')`, and the suite runs with the operator's own temp folder, so every suite run adds test records to the folder that the health readers and the research lanes read as real use. Separately, the scorer's printed start rate counts a document read with no write as a start, while the goal's fixed arm start rule calls that a lookup, and no printed number says how many starts are of that kind.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:64:A suite run leaves the shared metrics folder untouched, and each start rate prints the shape of its starts so a reader can apply either rule without rescoring.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:73:$ TMPDIR=<fresh dir> npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md:74:after TMPDIR run 729; files under per-run dir 5\n=====\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:2:title: \"Acceptance Criteria: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:5:  - \"untuned arm arena run acceptance criteria\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:19:      session_id: \"scaffold-033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:26:# Acceptance Criteria: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:40:**Packet:** 033-untuned-arm-arena-run\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/acceptance-criteria.md:56:| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given five arenas at `AC`, When every turn ends, Then each arena reads no remote and an empty status and every run line reads `restored: true` | Every arena ended at b765c7a14c5 with 0 remotes and an empty status (scratch/arenas-after.txt, the post-run check); 397 of 401 lines read restored true, the 4 fresh-skill-04 head-move lines read false (ADR-001) | Waived | ADR-001 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:2:title: \"Decision Record: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:3:description: \"Decisions taken without the operator during the untuned arm run: keeping the run when the sk-git row moved an arena's head, against the plan's rollback rule, and waiving the every-line-restored criterion for its four turns.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:5:  - \"033-untuned-arm-arena-run decisions\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:13:    recent_action: \"Recorded the decision to keep the run when one sk-git row moved an arena head\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:25:# Decision Record: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/decision-record.md:37:| ADR-001 | Keep and score the run instead of discarding it when the four `fresh-skill-04` turns read `restored: false` (devin off run 1 twice, devin on run 1, dsh on run 1), and waive AC-001's every-line-restored clause for those four turns only. Each turn moved the arena's head with a rebase, and the runner stops on a head move before it restores. Each arena was restored by hand to `b765c7a14c5` and checked clean with no remote, and the row was not rerun past one try. The hand restore left a `main` ref in the devin and dsh arenas that a fresh arena never has (created by devin's first turn, recreated in dsh). Later turns in those two arenas ran with it, and it was deleted after the run (`scratch/arenas-after.txt`). The deciding dsh decline line ran before dsh's head move. The row stays in the scorer's counts, scored as capped on the on arm. | `fresh-skill-04` is a skill-only row whose expected top is `sk-git`, so a history operation may be the task it asks for, not an escape. Discarding 401 lines over one row the runner cannot measure would have thrown away the other 35 rows on every runtime. D1 says take the safe default without asking. | AC-001 and REQ-001 as written, plan.md section 3 invariant (every line reads `restored: true`) and plan.md section 7 rollback trigger (any line with `restored` not true) for these four turns | `scratch/devin-rebase-evidence.txt`, `scratch/dsh-head-move-evidence.txt`, `scratch/reruns.txt`, `scratch/arenas-after.txt`, goal log rows on the devin rebase |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:2:title: \"Implementation Summary: Phase 33: untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:3:description: \"The untuned behaviour arm ran live on five runtimes in arenas at one commit and was scored: pooled gained 25 and lost 15 rows (p 0.0769), and dsh started a command on one decline row, so the verdict is Not shown and the B-5 trigger fired.\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:5:  - \"untuned arm arena run implementation summary\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:18:      - \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/arm-evidence.txt\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/implementation-summary.md:19:      - \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/scratch/summary-arm.json\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"TMPDIR\\\\|temp folder\\\\|metrics folder\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/*.md | head -20; echo =====; grep -rn \\\"buffer\\\\|listing\\\\|arena\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/033-untuned-arm-arena-run/*.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794815956934,"end":1794815957914}}}}
