 with that environment exits non-zero with stderr naming `transport 'ssh' not allowed`. Run the test and see the field undefined. Then in `R`'s `childEnv` set `env.GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL = 'file'`, and change the comments at lines 610 to 613, 1285 to 1288 and line 35 so the push boundary they name is the credential overrides and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file`, which keeps SSH and HTTPS out of reach whatever keys `HOME` holds. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `node $V5/remote-guard.mjs` prints the lines of `probes-after.txt`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T047.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n - [x] T048 State the stale rule and the transport boundary in the routing-accuracy README (`RA`). After T047, added by the coordinator from the T039 review (Q6). A doc task. In the paragraph at line 111 and the `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` row at line 143, say `stale_build` fires when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside it, and name the absolute-link refusal. In the `run-command-behaviour.mjs` row at line 137 say a live turn runs with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file`. Verify: `rg -c 'include' $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c 'GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL' $RA` prints 1, `DOCV $RA` exits 0, and `G diff -U0 -- $RA | rg '^\\+' | rg -c '\\x{2014}'` prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier FAIL then fixed by T048a (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T048.md): lines 137 and 143 correct, include and GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL present, DOCV 0 issues; line 111 framed the absolute-link refusal as an outside link, fixed in T048a\n - [x] T048a Correct the absolute-link clause on line 111 of the routing-accuracy README (`RA`). After T048. A doc task. In line 111 replace `resolves outside the source, including an absolute link that 