PK/review/review-report-pass-4.md`). After T041. Rerun `node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs --loop-type review --artifact-dir $PK/review` so the merged registry holds rounds `5b` and `5c`. Move the pass-four report with `G mv $PK/review/review-report.md $PK/review/review-report-pass-4.md`. Write a new `review-report.md` in the shape of the pass-four report: the scope, the lineages and their models, counts computed from the pass-five lineages only with `jq -r '[.openFindings[] | select(any(._lineages[]?; tostring | test(\"-5(b|c)?$\")))] | group_by(.severity) | map(\"\\(.[0].severity) \\(length)\") | join(\", \")' $PK/review/deep-review-findings-registry.json`, the verifier's verdict on each finding from `verify-5/report.md`, the adjudication of T039 and T041, one table row per finding with its task, its decision or its reason, and the remote-guard row's severity as the verifier graded it with the registry's P1 named. Name as a known limit that the merged registry keeps active rows of earlier passes, so its `activeP1` count is not this pass's count. Verify: `rg -c -F 'Pass Five' $PK/review/review-report.md` prints at least 1, `ls $PK/review/review-report-pass-4.md` prints the path, the report states 0 open P0 and 0 open P1 or names each open one with its reason, and every finding id of `verify-5/report.md` appears in it. Evidence: fanout-merge read 30 lineages; review-report-pass-4.md moved with git mv; new review-report.md: Pass Five count 1, pass-five jq counts P1 3, P2 45 explained, 0 open P0 and 0 open P1 stated, every verify-5 finding id present, the merged activeP1 of 15 named as a known limit\n-- [ ] T043 [C] Write the results and close the phase (`$PH/implementation-summary.md`, the parent spec phase 32 rows, the parent goal log through `PLOG` only). After T042. Copy `$SP/implementation-summary.scaffold.md` to `$PH/implementation-summary.md` and fill it: `BASE`, `FIX` and any later fix commit, the files changed, the probe lines before and after, the floors, the suite counts, every moved stored figure with its rule, the review verdict, the rounds and the synthesis, every `[B]` task and the items of `plan.md` D13. Recheck each file and line D13 cites with `rg -n` and correct a line number that moved. Mark each row of `acceptance-criteria.md` with the evidence observed, set the status in `spec.md` and the phase 32 rows of `../spec.md` to `Complete`, write `PLOG \"Phase 032 review pass five remediation | Complete | <FIX>: <one line>\"`, then run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder $PH --apply`. Commit `$PH`, `$PK/review/` and the parent `spec.md`, `goal.md`, `graph-metadata.json` and `description.json` by path with a conventional message and a second `-m` prose body. Then, on the clean tree the commit leaves, build one arena from this checkout with `node $B --source . --dest \"$T/arena\"`, `T` a `probe-032` folder removed in the same command. When it prints `stale_build`, run each named package's rebuild, which `system-spec-kit/runtime/dist` will need after T015, and build once more. When the second build still refuses, stop and mark the task `[B]` with its output. Write the result with `PLOG \"Arena build on the committed tree | <ok or the refusal> | <the copied count and trackedDotenv>\"` and commit `$PK/goal.md` by path. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $PH --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`, `rg -c \"\\| Unmet \\|\" $PH/acceptance-criteria.md` prints nothing, the arena build on the committed tree prints `\"ok\":true` with `trackedDotenv` naming the two tracked `.env.example` files, `LEFT` prints 0 and `G status --porcelain -- $PH $PK/review $PK/goal.md` prints nothing.\n+- [B] T043 [C] Write the results and close the phase (`$PH/implementation-summary.md`, the parent spec phase 32 rows, the parent goal log through `PLOG` only). After T042. Copy `$SP/implementation-summary.scaffold.md` to `$PH/implementation-summary.md` and fill it: `BASE`, `FIX` and any later fix commit, the files changed, the probe lines before and after, the floors, the suite counts, every moved stored figure with its rule, the review verdict, the rounds and the synthesis, every `[B]` task and the items of `plan.md` D13. Recheck each file and line D13 cites with `rg -n` and correct a line number that moved. Mark each row of `acceptance-criteria.md` with the evidence observed, set the status in `spec.md` and the phase 32 rows of `../spec.md` to `Complete`, write `PLOG \"Phase 032 review pass five remediation | Complete | <FIX>: <one line>\"`, then run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder $PH --apply`. Commit `$PH`, `$PK/review/` and the parent `spec.md`, `goal.md`, `graph-metadata.json` and `description.json` by path with a conventional message and a second `-m` prose body. Then, on the clean tree the commit leaves, build one arena from this checkout with `node $B --source . --dest \"$T/arena\"`, `T` a `probe-032` folder removed in the same command. When it prints `stale_build`, run each named package's rebuild, which `system-spec-kit/runtime/dist` will need after T015, and build once more. When the second build still refuses, stop and mark the task `[B]` with its output. Write the result with `PLOG \"Arena build on the committed tree | <ok or the refusal> | <the copied count and trackedDotenv>\"` and commit `$PK/goal.md` by path. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $PH --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`, `rg -c \"\\| Unmet \\|\" $PH/acceptance-criteria.md` prints nothing, the arena build on the committed tree prints `\"ok\":true` with `trackedDotenv` naming the two tracked `.env.example` files, `LEFT` prints 0 and `G status --porcelain -- $PH $PK/review $PK/goal.md` prints nothing. Blocked 2026-11-15: the committed tree `ddb12a6852c` built first with `stale_build` on `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/d