{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816538355,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e36694b9002jsLg3MUkKa95qn","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e3668c160018VQcV9U2aPN8Pk","type":"tool","id":"call_a92ac1b530bd43b89718a8b6","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Strategy - arena-config pass six\n\n## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder review, pass six).\n- Lineage area: `arena-config` — the three paths `review/review-scope-6.txt` assigns to this label: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `vitest.config.ts`.\n- Diff under review: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff ddb12a6852c 85550ee946e -- <path>`; 62 insertions, 1 deletion across the three files.\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\n- Operator focus: the text bound as `reviewFocus` in `deep-review-config.json`, reproduced in every iteration.\n- Stop conditions: legal convergence per `convergence.cjs`, or `maxIterations=3`.\n- Success criteria: every changed line read against its claim, each finding carrying file:line and a concrete input, holdout hygiene preserved, no code changed.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nTwo changed behaviours. `vitest.config.ts` makes one temp folder per suite run and points `TMPDIR` at it, so the advisor's durable health records (`lib/metrics.ts` `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT`) stop landing in the operator's shared metrics folder. `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` raises the git helper's `maxBuffer` to 512 MiB so a whole-repository listing no longer aborts the arena build with `spawn_failed`, and `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` gains the 6,000-file regression case that proves it.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n\n- [x] D1 Correctness\n- [x] D2 Security\n- [x] D3 Traceability\n- [x] D4 Maintainability\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not re-reporting the recorded limits named by `review/review-brief-6.txt` without a new input that breaks them.\n- Not reviewing the scorer, merge-docs or other areas' files except as evidence for a claim about these three.\n- Not running the vitest suites, the arena builder or any repo tooling that writes outside the lineage folder; the buffer behaviour is reproduced with `spawnSync` directly instead.\n- Not opening `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`, and not reading any prompt corpus except through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`.\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Legal convergence from `convergence.cjs` with every quality gate passing.\n- `maxIterationsReached` after iteration 3, with synthesis stating partial coverage honestly.\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| correctness | PASS | 1 | The raised buffer removes the ENOBUFS abort; two cleanup/portability limits remain as P2. |\n| traceability | PASS | 2 | Spec, task and checklist claims match the code; the isolation lever is missing from the stress config. |\n| maintainability | PASS | 3 | Test premise and ENOBUFS diagnosis are the two remaining efficiency costs. |\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 4 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +2 P0, +0 P1, +2 P2 in iteration 1; +1 P2 in iteration 2; +1 P2 in iteration 3\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- [Direct reproduction of the buffer premise]: spawning `git ls-files -z` with and without `maxBuffer` on a 6,000-file fixture reproduced `{status:null,error:\"ENOBUFS\"}` and `{status:0, stdoutBytes:1116018}` in one step, which settles the fix's premise without running the suite (iteration 1).\n- [Claim-to-constant reading]: reading `lib/metrics.ts:185` beside the config block proved the lever reaches the durable root and that `tmpdir()` is the only switch (iteration 1).\n- [Task-row evidence audit]: reading T053 and T043 beside the code showed the fix's recorded first-run failure and its final `ok:true` build, which closes the traceability question without a live run (iteration 2).\n- [Entry-point enumeration]: listing every `vitest*.config.ts` and every workflow that runs it exposed the one suite path the isolation never reaches (iteration 2).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- [Assuming the suite has one config]: the first pass reasoned about `vitest.config.ts` alone; the stress workflow runs `vitest.stress.config.ts`, which cost a second pass to find (iteration 2).\n- [Treating the config comment as the contract]: the comment's \"every process a test spawns inherits it\" is narrower in practice than it reads, because a child spawned with an explicit env object drops `TMPDIR` (iteration 2).\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n- [A truncated listing read as success]: `git()` throws on `result.error`, so an `ENOBUFS` read never reaches a caller as a short list (iteration 1).\n- [A directory-listing escape through the raised cap]: `maxBuffer` bounds bytes read, not paths written; the copy and symlink guards are unchanged by the diff (iteration 1).\n- [Windows `TEMP`/`TMP` inheritance]: no Windows runner, no `win32` branch in the advisor runtime, and the one `describe.skipIf(win32)` shows the suite does not target it (iteration 1).\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: correctness, traceability, maintainability\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- [Truncated git output read as complete]: `git()` raises `StepFailure` on `result.error`, so a buffer overflow can never reach `staleBuilds` or `trackedDotenvFiles` as a short list (iteration 1).\n- [A buffer cap that changes copy or symlink safety]: the cap bounds the bytes git prints; `copyPath`, `escapingLinks` and `stampBuildTree` are untouched by the diff (iteration 1).\n- [A per-run temp folder that breaks socket paths]: `launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs` relocates a socket dir above the 104-byte `sun_path` limit, and the advisor's default socket dir is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`, not `tmpdir()` (iteration 1).\n- [A duplicate write into the shared metrics folder from the default suite]: `advisorHookOutcomesPath` resolves under `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT`, which is computed from `tmpdir()` at import, and the config sets `TMPDIR` before any worker starts (iteration 2).\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n\n- Dimension: none remaining — all three dimensions covered, 4 P2 advisories, no active P0 or P1.\n- Focus area: synthesis only.\n- Reason: `maxIterations=3` reached with every dimension reviewed and no finding above P2.\n- Rotation status: complete.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — direct reproduction was the cheapest evidence for both changes.\n- Required evidence: the terminal convergence decision, the reducer's registry and the synthesis report.\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:5-18`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:142-152`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:753-789`.\n- Behaviour claims: a suite run leaves the shared metrics folder untouched (`035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md` REQ-001, AC-001, AC-005); the arena builder can read a whole-repository listing (`032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md` T053); the arena build succeeds on the committed tree (T043).\n- Reuse and conventions: `lib/metrics.ts:185` `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT`, `os.tmpdir()` reading `TMPDIR` on POSIX; `spawnSync` `maxBuffer` default; the `git()`/`gitText()` failure shape.\n- Review risks and gaps: no suite run and no arena build in this lineage, because both write outside the lineage folder; the buffer premise is reproduced with a direct `spawnSync` probe instead.\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 2 | Phase 035's REQ-001 and phase 032's T053/T043 read against the changed lines; both match. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | 2 | 035's AC-001 and AC-005 carry observed evidence; 032's T053 names the failing first run and T043 names the `ok:true` build. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | The skill entry files are not part of this area's diff. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No agent definition is in scope for this area. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No feature-catalog leaf names these two behaviours. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | 2 | The manual playbook names the durable metrics folder as an operator inspection path; the stress-suite gap leaves that path reachable from one suite entry point. |\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | D1, D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 2 | 2 P2 | complete |\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 3\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-arena-config-6-1794815529929-dybl7p, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-16T08:08:13.000Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Deep Review Strategy - arena-config pass six\\n\\n## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\\n\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder review, pass six).\\n- Lineage area: `arena-config` — the three paths `review/review-scope-6.txt` assigns to this label: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `vitest.config.ts`.\\n- Diff under review: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff ddb12a6852c 85550ee946e -- <path>`; 62 insertions, 1 deletion across the three files.\\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability.\\n- Operator focus: the text bound as `reviewFocus` in `deep-review-config.json`, reproduced in every iteration.\\n- Stop conditions: legal convergence per `convergence.cjs`, or `maxIterations=3`.\\n- Success criteria: every changed line read against its claim, each finding carrying file:line and a concrete input, holdout hygiene preserved, no code changed.\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nTwo changed behaviours. `vitest.config.ts` makes one temp folder per suite run and points `TMPDIR` at it, so the advisor's durable health records (`lib/metrics.ts` `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT`) stop landing in the operator's shared metrics folder. `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` raises the git helper's `maxBuffer` to 512 MiB so a whole-repository listing no longer aborts the arena build with `spawn_failed`, and `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` gains the 6,000-file regression case that proves it.\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [x] D1 Correctness\\n- [x] D2 Security\\n- [x] D3 Traceability\\n- [x] D4 Maintainability\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Not re-reporting the recorded limits named by `review/review-brief-6.txt` without a new input that breaks them.\\n- Not reviewing the scorer, merge-docs or other areas' files except as evidence for a claim about these three.\\n- Not running the vitest suites, the arena builder or any repo tooling that writes outside the lineage folder; the buffer behaviour is reproduced with `spawnSync` directly instead.\\n- Not opening `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`, and not reading any prompt corpus except through `jq 'del(.prompt)'`.\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Legal convergence from `convergence.cjs` with every quality gate passing.\\n- `maxIterationsReached` after iteration 3, with synthesis stating partial coverage honestly.\\n\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n| correctness | PASS | 1 | The raised buffer removes the ENOBUFS abort; two cleanup/portability limits remain as P2. |\\n| traceability | PASS | 2 | Spec, task and checklist claims match the code; the isolation lever is missing from the stress config. |\\n| maintainability | PASS | 3 | Test premise and ENOBUFS diagnosis are the two remaining efficiency costs. |\\n\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 4 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +2 P0, +0 P1, +2 P2 in iteration 1; +1 P2 in iteration 2; +1 P2 in iteration 3\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- [Direct reproduction of the buffer premise]: spawning `git ls-files -z` with and without `maxBuffer` on a 6,000-file fixture reproduced `{status:null,error:\\\"ENOBUFS\\\"}` and `{status:0, stdoutBytes:1116018}` in one step, which settles the fix's premise without running the suite (iteration 1).\\n- [Claim-to-constant reading]: reading `lib/metrics.ts:185` beside the config block proved the lever reaches the durable root and that `tmpdir()` is the only switch (iteration 1).\\n- [Task-row evidence audit]: reading T053 and T043 beside the code showed the fix's recorded first-run failure and its final `ok:true` build, which closes the traceability question without a live run (iteration 2).\\n- [Entry-point enumeration]: listing every `vitest*.config.ts` and every workflow that runs it exposed the one suite path the isolation never reaches (iteration 2).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- [Assuming the suite has one config]: the first pass reasoned about `vitest.config.ts` alone; the stress workflow runs `vitest.stress.config.ts`, which cost a second pass to find (iteration 2).\\n- [Treating the config comment as the contract]: the comment's \\\"every process a test spawns inherits it\\\" is narrower in practice than it reads, because a child spawned with an explicit env object drops `TMPDIR` (iteration 2).\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n- [A truncated listing read as success]: `git()` throws on `result.error`, so an `ENOBUFS` read never reaches a caller as a short list (iteration 1).\\n- [A directory-listing escape through the raised cap]: `maxBuffer` bounds bytes read, not paths written; the copy and symlink guards are unchanged by the diff (iteration 1).\\n- [Windows `TEMP`/`TMP` inheritance]: no Windows runner, no `win32` branch in the advisor runtime, and the one `describe.skipIf(win32)` shows the suite does not target it (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: correctness, traceability, maintainability\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- [Truncated git output read as complete]: `git()` raises `StepFailure` on `result.error`, so a buffer overflow can never reach `staleBuilds` or `trackedDotenvFiles` as a short list (iteration 1).\\n- [A buffer cap that changes copy or symlink safety]: the cap bounds the bytes git prints; `copyPath`, `escapingLinks` and `stampBuildTree` are untouched by the diff (iteration 1).\\n- [A per-run temp folder that breaks socket paths]: `launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs` relocates a socket dir above the 104-byte `sun_path` limit, and the advisor's default socket dir is `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`, not `tmpdir()` (iteration 1).\\n- [A duplicate write into the shared metrics folder from the default suite]: `advisorHookOutcomesPath` resolves under `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT`, which is computed from `tmpdir()` at import, and the config sets `TMPDIR` before any worker starts (iteration 2).\\n\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining — all three dimensions covered, 4 P2 advisories, no active P0 or P1.\\n- Focus area: synthesis only.\\n- Reason: `maxIterations=3` reached with every dimension reviewed and no finding above P2.\\n- Rotation status: complete.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — direct reproduction was the cheapest evidence for both changes.\\n- Required evidence: the terminal convergence decision, the reducer's registry and the synthesis report.\\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:5-18`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:142-152`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:753-789`.\\n- Behaviour claims: a suite run leaves the shared metrics folder untouched (`035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/spec.md` REQ-001, AC-001, AC-005); the arena builder can read a whole-repository listing (`032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md` T053); the arena build succeeds on the committed tree (T043).\\n- Reuse and conventions: `lib/metrics.ts:185` `DURABLE_METRICS_ROOT`, `os.tmpdir()` reading `TMPDIR` on POSIX; `spawnSync` `maxBuffer` default; the `git()`/`gitText()` failure shape.\\n- Review risks and gaps: no suite run and no arena build in this lineage, because both write outside the lineage folder; the buffer premise is reproduced with a direct `spawnSync` probe instead.\\n\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 2 | Phase 035's REQ-001 and phase 032's T053/T043 read against the changed lines; both match. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | 2 | 035's AC-001 and AC-005 carry observed evidence; 032's T053 names the failing first run and T043 names the `ok:true` build. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | The skill entry files are not part of this area's diff. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No agent definition is in scope for this area. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No feature-catalog leaf names these two behaviours. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial | 2 | The manual playbook names the durable metrics folder as an operator inspection path; the stress-suite gap leaves that path reachable from one suite entry point. |\\n\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | D1, D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 2 | 2 P2 | complete |\\n\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- Max iterations: 3\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-arena-config-6-1794815529929-dybl7p, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\\n- Per-iteration budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Severity threshold: P2\\n- Review target type: spec-folder\\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\\n- Started: 2026-11-16T08:08:13.000Z\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816513209,"end":1794816538355}}}}
