{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816771642,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e36a7984002BTxBHurVEngv1r","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e36a6045001XMzxd4UwZ6pRIN","type":"tool","id":"call_a7ab339d3697467597147adc","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"- [Task-row evidence audit]: reading T053 and T043 beside the code showed the fix's recorded first-run failure and its final `ok:true` build, which closes the traceability question without a live run (iteration 2).\n- [Entry-point enumeration]: listing every `vitest*.config.ts` and every workflow that runs it exposed the one suite path the isolation never reaches (iteration 2).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- [Assuming the suite has one config]: the first pass reasoned about `vitest.config.ts` alone; the stress workflow runs `vitest.stress.config.ts`, which cost a second pass to find (iteration 2).\n- [Treating the config comment as the contract]: the comment's \"every process a test spawns inherits it\" is narrower in practice than it reads, because a child spawned with an explicit env object drops `TMPDIR` (iteration 2).","newString":"- [Signal-exit probe]: a four-line Node script with an `exit` listener, killed with `SIGTERM`, wrote no marker while the same script ending through `process.exit(0)` did, which settled the cleanup claim without touching the runner (iteration 1).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- [Assuming one cleanup path is enough]: the config's comment reads as \"the run removes it on exit\", but the listener covers one of several ways a run ends; the gap cost the rest of the pass a second reading of Node's exit contract (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -51,15 +51,13 @@\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - [Direct reproduction of the buffer premise]: spawning `git ls-files -z` with and without `maxBuffer` on a 6,000-file fixture reproduced `{status:null,error:\"ENOBUFS\"}` and `{status:0, stdoutBytes:1116018}` in one step, which settles the fix's premise without running the suite (iteration 1).\n - [Claim-to-constant reading]: reading `lib/metrics.ts:185` beside the config block proved the lever reaches the durable root and that `tmpdir()` is the only switch (iteration 1).\n-- [Task-row evidence audit]: reading T053 and T043 beside the code showed the fix's recorded first-run failure and its final `ok:true` build, which closes the traceability question without a live run (iteration 2).\n-- [Entry-point enumeration]: listing every `vitest*.config.ts` and every workflow that runs it exposed the one suite path the isolation never reaches (iteration 2).\n+- [Signal-exit probe]: a four-line Node script with an `exit` listener, killed with `SIGTERM`, wrote no marker while the same script ending through `process.exit(0)` did, which settled the cleanup claim without touching the runner (iteration 1).\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-- [Assuming the suite has one config]: the first pass reasoned about `vitest.config.ts` alone; the stress workflow runs `vitest.stress.config.ts`, which cost a second pass to find (iteration 2).\n-- [Treating the config comment as the contract]: the comment's \"every process a test spawns inherits it\" is narrower in practice than it reads, because a child spawned with an explicit env object drops `TMPDIR` (iteration 2).\n+- [Assuming one cleanup path is enough]: the config's comment reads as \"the run removes it on exit\", but the listener covers one of several ways a run ends; the gap cost the rest of the pass a second reading of Node's exit contract (iteration 1).\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n ### A listing truncated by the default buffer reaching a caller as a complete list: `git()` throws before returning. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":4}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"- [Task-row evidence audit]: reading T053 and T043 beside the code showed the fix's recorded first-run failure and its final `ok:true` build, which closes the traceability question without a live run (iteration 2).\\n- [Entry-point enumeration]: listing every `vitest*.config.ts` and every workflow that runs it exposed the one suite path the isolation never reaches (iteration 2).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- [Assuming the suite has one config]: the first pass reasoned about `vitest.config.ts` alone; the stress workflow runs `vitest.stress.config.ts`, which cost a second pass to find (iteration 2).\\n- [Treating the config comment as the contract]: the comment's \\\"every process a test spawns inherits it\\\" is narrower in practice than it reads, because a child spawned with an explicit env object drops `TMPDIR` (iteration 2).\",\"newString\":\"- [Signal-exit probe]: a four-line Node script with an `exit` listener, killed with `SIGTERM`, wrote no marker while the same script ending through `process.exit(0)` did, which settled the cleanup claim without touching the runner (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- [Assuming one cleanup path is enough]: the config's comment reads as \\\"the run removes it on exit\\\", but the listener covers one of several ways a run ends; the gap cost the rest of the pass a second reading of Node's exit contract (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816768388,"end":1794816771642}}}}
