e cleanup path is enough]: the config's comment reads as \"the run removes it on exit\", but the listener covers one of several ways a run ends; the gap cost the rest of the pass a second reading of Node's exit contract (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -51,12 +51,16 @@\n \n - [Direct reproduction of the buffer premise]: spawning `git ls-files -z` with and without `maxBuffer` on a 6,000-file fixture reproduced `{status:null,error:\"ENOBUFS\"}` and `{status:0, stdoutBytes:1116018}` in one step, which settles the fix's premise without running the suite (iteration 1).\n - [Claim-to-constant reading]: reading `lib/metrics.ts:185` beside the config block proved the lever reaches the durable root and that `tmpdir()` is the only switch (iteration 1).\n - [Signal-exit probe]: a four-line Node script with an `exit` listener, killed with `SIGTERM`, wrote no marker while the same script ending through `process.exit(0)` did, which settled the cleanup claim without touching the runner (iteration 1).\n+- [Task-row evidence audit]: reading T053 and T043 beside the code showed the fix's recorded first-run failure and its final `ok:true` build, which closes the traceability question without a live run (iteration 2).\n+- [Entry-point enumeration]: listing every `vitest*.config.ts` under the runtime and every workflow that runs one exposed the single suite path the isolation never reaches (iteration 2).\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - [Assuming one cleanup path is enough]: the config's comment reads as \"the run removes it on exit\", but the listener covers one of several ways a run ends; the gap cost the rest of the pass a second reading of Node's exit contract (iteration 1).\n+- [Assuming the suite has one config]: the first pass reasoned about `vitest.config.ts` alone; the stress workflow runs `vitest.stress.config.ts`, which cost a second pass to find (iteration 2).\n+- [Treating the summary sentence as the spec]: `implementation-summary.md:64` is broader than the spec it summarises, and only reading the spec's own scope list showed that the sentence, not the task, is what overstates (iteration 2).\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n ### A listing truncated by the default buffer reaching a caller as a complete list: `git()` throws before returning. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- [Signal-exit probe]: a four-line Node script with an `exit` listener, killed with `SIGTERM`, wrote no marker while the same script ending through `process.exit(0)` did, which settled the cleanup claim without touching the runner (iteration 1).\\n- [Task-row evidence audit]: reading T053 and T043 beside the code showed the fix's recorded first-run failure and its final `ok:true` build, which closes the traceability question without a live run (iteration 2).\\n- [Entry-point enumeration]: listing every `vitest*.config.ts` under the runtime and every workflow that runs one exposed the single suite path the isolation never reaches (iteration 2).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- [Assuming one cleanup path is enough]: the config's comment reads as \\\"the run removes it on exit\\\", but the listener covers one of several ways a run ends; the gap cost the rest of the pass a second reading of Node's exit contract (iteration 1).\\n- [Assuming the suite has one config]: the first pass reasoned about `vitest.config.ts` alone; the stress workflow runs `vitest.stress.config.ts`, which cost a second pass to find (iteration 2).\\n- [Treating the summary sentence as the spec]: `implementation-summary.md:64` is broader than the spec it summarises, and only reading the spec's own scope list showed that the sentence, not the task, is what overstates (iteration 2).\",\"oldString\":\"- [Signal-exit probe]: a four-line Node script with an `exit` listener, killed with `SIGTERM`, wrote no marker while the same script ending through `process.exit(0)` did, which settled the cleanup claim without touching the runner (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- [Assuming one cleanup path is enough]: the config's comment reads as \\\"the run removes it on exit\\\", but the listener covers one of several ways a run ends; the gap cost the rest of the pass a second reading of Node's exit contract (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816922292,"end":1794816926165}}}}
