{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794816996465,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e36d8ddd001XQeLLJyhtHJMjL","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e36d8293001ALRNLte5AN2cuK","type":"tool","id":"call_c98e4fb41d1746f58e53aa87","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dimension\n\nPrimary dimension: **maintainability**, with a **security** read of the same two paths. The maintainability question is what the next reader pays to trust or diagnose these two changes; the security question is whether the new temp folder or the raised read cap widened anything the code already bounds.\n\nReview focus addressed: the operator focus binds this area's three files and the pass-six brief. This iteration re-read the changed lines in the arena builder and in the new regression test, asked what evidence each carries for the next maintainer, and checked the two security-relevant boundaries the changes touch — the privacy mode of the per-run folder and the dotenv filter in the arena copy. No other area's files were opened, no recorded limit was restated, no prompt corpus was opened and `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` was not read.\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `arena-config-6`.\n- Session: `fanout-arena-config-6-1794815529929-dybl7p`, generation 1, lineage mode new.\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6`.\n- Budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes.\n- Doctrine: `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md` loaded before severity calls.\n- Sources read for this pass: the three scope files at `85550ee946e`, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts:451-466`, and the T043 blocked-run record that named the `ENOBUFS` message.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755-789` (and `471-509` for the block's helpers)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:142-152`, `:358-385` (the dotenv and link boundaries the cap does not touch)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:9-18`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:451-466` (the writer whose records the folder holds)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:116` and `:164` (the blocked run and the repair)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The buffer regression test never asserts the premise it guards** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755-789` -- The test's name and comment say the listing passes the default buffer, but the body only builds the fixture and asserts `built.status === 0` with `ok: true`. Nothing measures the listing, so the test passes unchanged if the fixture shrinks below 1 MiB, and it would also pass if the builder stopped reading the listing at all.\n   - Case: a maintainer trims the loop from 6,000 files to 3,000 to shorten the test; the listing becomes 558,018 bytes, well under the 1,048,576-byte default cap, and the test still passes while the overflow it was written for is no longer exercised.\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:765-766]` (the fixture loop and its single 171-character name), `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:786-788]` (the two assertions); measured: the fixture prints 1,116,018 bytes, which is 67,442 bytes past the cap.\n   - User impact: the suite would keep reporting a passing regression test for a buffer that no longer has anything over it, so a future shrink of the cap or of the fixture loses the guard silently.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: the assertion set is the whole test body; no other case in the `arena builder` block measures a listing (`rg -n \"ls-files\" tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` returns only this test's helper calls).\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"command-behaviour-guards arena builder block\", \"prepare-behaviour-arena git buffer\", \"regression coverage\"]\n   - Recommendation: assert the listing size before building — `spawnSync('git', ['ls-files','-z'], { cwd: source, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 8 * 1024 * 1024 }).stdout.length` greater than `1024 * 1024` — so the premise is part of the test.\n\n2. **A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:150` -- `git()` turns every `result.error` into `StepFailure('spawn_failed', …)`, including `ENOBUFS`. Above the new cap the operator therefore reads the same code and message a missing `git` binary produces, and the packet's own history shows how that reads: T043 was blocked for a day on `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs: spawn_failed: spawnSync git ENOBUFS`, and the note records the string without naming the buffer as the cause.\n   - Case: a monorepo whose `git ls-files -z` reaches about 512 MiB (roughly 2.7 million 190-byte paths) builds an arena; the builder prints `{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"spawn_failed\"}` and the operator starts by checking whether `git` is installed or on `PATH`, which is the opposite of the real cause.\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:148-150]`; `[SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:164]` (the blocked-run note quoting the same string).\n   - User impact: the one diagnosis this fix was written to remove is still the diagnosis above the cap, so a future ceiling raise repeats the same blocked investigation.\n   - Finding class: instance-only\n   - Scope proof: `result.error` is read in exactly one place in the builder (`rg -n \"result.error\" prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` returns `git()` and `runCp()`); `runCp` is a copy failure and keeps `copy_failed`, so the git path is the whole class.\n   - Affected surface hints: [\"prepare-behaviour-arena git()\", \"arena builder failure codes\", \"operator diagnosis\"]\n   - Recommendation: branch on `result.error.code === 'ENOBUFS'` and throw `StepFailure('listing_too_large', 'git output passed the 512 MiB buffer')`, leaving every other `result.error` as `spawn_failed`.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Re-checked for this pass: the two changed behaviours still match phase 035's REQ-001 and phase 032's T053; neither new finding contradicts a stated requirement, both are within the delivery. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | Carried from iteration 2: T002, AC-001, AC-005, T053 and T043 each record observed evidence for the delivered behaviour. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:451-466` — the record writer the per-run folder holds; the records are prompt-free unless `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:358-385` — `escapingLinks`, the copy boundary the raised cap does not touch.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:475-487` — `copyPath`, which skips every `.env*` file in the copied build trees.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:164` — the blocked-run note that quotes `spawn_failed: spawnSync git ENOBUFS`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The 512 MiB ceiling was not exercised: reaching it would need about 2.7 million paths, and no fixture in the repository is that large. The finding is therefore about the diagnosis of the ceiling, not about a reproduced run above it.\n- The test-premise finding assumes the fixture could shrink without a reviewer noticing; that is exactly the maintenance risk, not a present defect, so it stays P2.\n- Security was checked on the two boundaries the diff touches and not widened into a third dimension: the temp folder is created by `mkdtempSync` with mode `0700` (observed), and the dotenv filter in the copy is unchanged by the diff.\n- `runCp` keeps its own `copy_failed` code, so the `spawn_failed` confusion is specific to the git path and is not a class over every spawn in the builder.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The per-run folder is private: `mkdtempSync` creates it mode `0700` (observed on this machine), and `metrics.ts` still tightens the metrics directory and log files it writes inside it, so moving the records into a `sav-*` folder does not loosen their mode.\n- The raised read cap does not widen any write path: `copyPlan`, `copyPath`, `escapingLinks` and `stampBuildTree` are unchanged, and the dotenv filter still runs over every copied build tree.\n- The new test's fixture is deterministic: one 171-character base name plus a four-digit prefix produces the same 1,116,018-byte listing every run, which matches the size T053 recorded.\n- The builder's failure shapes stay separated on the copy path: `runCp` reports `copy_failed`, and only `git()` reports `spawn_failed`.\n- No scope violation occurred: writes stayed inside the lineage directory.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A private-mode regression from moving the health records: `mkdtempSync` creates `0700`, and the writers still set `0700`/`0600` on what they create.\n- A dotenv leak reintroduced through the larger read: the cap bounds bytes printed by git; the copy filter is a separate walk and is unchanged.\n- A fixture that is flaky in size: the name length and the count are both literals, and the byte size is reproducible.\n- An `ENOBUFS` confusion on the copy path: `runCp` maps its own failures to `copy_failed`.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: none remaining.\n- Focus area: synthesis only.\n- Reason: `maxIterations=3` is reached with correctness, traceability, maintainability and a security read of the changed boundaries covered; no active P0 or P1.\n- Rotation status: complete.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — the packet's own blocked-run note supplied the concrete input for the failure-code advisory.\n- Required evidence: the terminal convergence decision, the finding registry, and the synthesis report.\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nPrimary dimension: **maintainability**, with a **security** read of the same two paths. The maintainability question is what the next reader pays to trust or diagnose these two changes; the security question is whether the new temp folder or the raised read cap widened anything the code already bounds.\\n\\nReview focus addressed: the operator focus binds this area's three files and the pass-six brief. This iteration re-read the changed lines in the arena builder and in the new regression test, asked what evidence each carries for the next maintainer, and checked the two security-relevant boundaries the changes touch — the privacy mode of the per-run folder and the dotenv filter in the arena copy. No other area's files were opened, no recorded limit was restated, no prompt corpus was opened and `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` was not read.\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review, detached fan-out lineage `arena-config-6`.\\n- Session: `fanout-arena-config-6-1794815529929-dybl7p`, generation 1, lineage mode new.\\n- Artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6`.\\n- Budget: 60 tool calls, 10 minutes.\\n- Doctrine: `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/references/review-core.md` loaded before severity calls.\\n- Sources read for this pass: the three scope files at `85550ee946e`, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts:451-466`, and the T043 blocked-run record that named the `ENOBUFS` message.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755-789` (and `471-509` for the block's helpers)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:142-152`, `:358-385` (the dotenv and link boundaries the cap does not touch)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:9-18`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:451-466` (the writer whose records the folder holds)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:116` and `:164` (the blocked run and the repair)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The buffer regression test never asserts the premise it guards** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755-789` -- The test's name and comment say the listing passes the default buffer, but the body only builds the fixture and asserts `built.status === 0` with `ok: true`. Nothing measures the listing, so the test passes unchanged if the fixture shrinks below 1 MiB, and it would also pass if the builder stopped reading the listing at all.\\n   - Case: a maintainer trims the loop from 6,000 files to 3,000 to shorten the test; the listing becomes 558,018 bytes, well under the 1,048,576-byte default cap, and the test still passes while the overflow it was written for is no longer exercised.\\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:765-766]` (the fixture loop and its single 171-character name), `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:786-788]` (the two assertions); measured: the fixture prints 1,116,018 bytes, which is 67,442 bytes past the cap.\\n   - User impact: the suite would keep reporting a passing regression test for a buffer that no longer has anything over it, so a future shrink of the cap or of the fixture loses the guard silently.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: the assertion set is the whole test body; no other case in the `arena builder` block measures a listing (`rg -n \\\"ls-files\\\" tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` returns only this test's helper calls).\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"command-behaviour-guards arena builder block\\\", \\\"prepare-behaviour-arena git buffer\\\", \\\"regression coverage\\\"]\\n   - Recommendation: assert the listing size before building — `spawnSync('git', ['ls-files','-z'], { cwd: source, encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 8 * 1024 * 1024 }).stdout.length` greater than `1024 * 1024` — so the premise is part of the test.\\n\\n2. **A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:150` -- `git()` turns every `result.error` into `StepFailure('spawn_failed', …)`, including `ENOBUFS`. Above the new cap the operator therefore reads the same code and message a missing `git` binary produces, and the packet's own history shows how that reads: T043 was blocked for a day on `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs: spawn_failed: spawnSync git ENOBUFS`, and the note records the string without naming the buffer as the cause.\\n   - Case: a monorepo whose `git ls-files -z` reaches about 512 MiB (roughly 2.7 million 190-byte paths) builds an arena; the builder prints `{\\\"ok\\\":false,\\\"code\\\":\\\"spawn_failed\\\"}` and the operator starts by checking whether `git` is installed or on `PATH`, which is the opposite of the real cause.\\n   - Evidence: `[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:148-150]`; `[SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:164]` (the blocked-run note quoting the same string).\\n   - User impact: the one diagnosis this fix was written to remove is still the diagnosis above the cap, so a future ceiling raise repeats the same blocked investigation.\\n   - Finding class: instance-only\\n   - Scope proof: `result.error` is read in exactly one place in the builder (`rg -n \\\"result.error\\\" prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` returns `git()` and `runCp()`); `runCp` is a copy failure and keeps `copy_failed`, so the git path is the whole class.\\n   - Affected surface hints: [\\\"prepare-behaviour-arena git()\\\", \\\"arena builder failure codes\\\", \\\"operator diagnosis\\\"]\\n   - Recommendation: branch on `result.error.code === 'ENOBUFS'` and throw `StepFailure('listing_too_large', 'git output passed the 512 MiB buffer')`, leaving every other `result.error` as `spawn_failed`.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Re-checked for this pass: the two changed behaviours still match phase 035's REQ-001 and phase 032's T053; neither new finding contradicts a stated requirement, both are within the delivery. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | Carried from iteration 2: T002, AC-001, AC-005, T053 and T043 each record observed evidence for the delivered behaviour. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/metrics.ts:451-466` — the record writer the per-run folder holds; the records are prompt-free unless `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:358-385` — `escapingLinks`, the copy boundary the raised cap does not touch.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:475-487` — `copyPath`, which skips every `.env*` file in the copied build trees.\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:164` — the blocked-run note that quotes `spawn_failed: spawnSync git ENOBUFS`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The 512 MiB ceiling was not exercised: reaching it would need about 2.7 million paths, and no fixture in the repository is that large. The finding is therefore about the diagnosis of the ceiling, not about a reproduced run above it.\\n- The test-premise finding assumes the fixture could shrink without a reviewer noticing; that is exactly the maintenance risk, not a present defect, so it stays P2.\\n- Security was checked on the two boundaries the diff touches and not widened into a third dimension: the temp folder is created by `mkdtempSync` with mode `0700` (observed), and the dotenv filter in the copy is unchanged by the diff.\\n- `runCp` keeps its own `copy_failed` code, so the `spawn_failed` confusion is specific to the git path and is not a class over every spawn in the builder.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The per-run folder is private: `mkdtempSync` creates it mode `0700` (observed on this machine), and `metrics.ts` still tightens the metrics directory and log files it writes inside it, so moving the records into a `sav-*` folder does not loosen their mode.\\n- The raised read cap does not widen any write path: `copyPlan`, `copyPath`, `escapingLinks` and `stampBuildTree` are unchanged, and the dotenv filter still runs over every copied build tree.\\n- The new test's fixture is deterministic: one 171-character base name plus a four-digit prefix produces the same 1,116,018-byte listing every run, which matches the size T053 recorded.\\n- The builder's failure shapes stay separated on the copy path: `runCp` reports `copy_failed`, and only `git()` reports `spawn_failed`.\\n- No scope violation occurred: writes stayed inside the lineage directory.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A private-mode regression from moving the health records: `mkdtempSync` creates `0700`, and the writers still set `0700`/`0600` on what they create.\\n- A dotenv leak reintroduced through the larger read: the cap bounds bytes printed by git; the copy filter is a separate walk and is unchanged.\\n- A fixture that is flaky in size: the name length and the count are both literals, and the byte size is reproducible.\\n- An `ENOBUFS` confusion on the copy path: `runCp` maps its own failures to `copy_failed`.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: none remaining.\\n- Focus area: synthesis only.\\n- Reason: `maxIterations=3` is reached with correctness, traceability, maintainability and a security read of the changed boundaries covered; no active P0 or P1.\\n- Rotation status: complete.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: productive — the packet's own blocked-run note supplied the concrete input for the failure-code advisory.\\n- Required evidence: the terminal convergence decision, the finding registry, and the synthesis report.\\n- Recovery note: none; no failed iteration.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794816970205,"end":1794816996465}}}}
