{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794817215021,"sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","part":{"partID":"prt_1e370cddd001tt4WhUP8CWjNih","sessionID":"ses_e1ca84eaaffePZ4Vo82UrPH517","messageID":"msg_1e370b3fa001jHLI6JC08IcqbL","type":"tool","id":"call_d03e38991dc5476494817ea8","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report — arena-config pass six\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict: PASS**\n- **hasAdvisories: true** — five active P2 findings, no active P0 or P1.\n- **P0/P1/P2 counts: 0 / 0 / 5** — the counts `review-verdict.cjs` derived from the lineage registry and state log, which are the counts this report uses.\n- **Review scope**: the three paths `review/review-scope-6.txt` assigns to the `arena-config` area, diffed with the scope file's per-area command over `ddb12a6852c..85550ee946e`: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `vitest.config.ts` (62 insertions, 1 deletion).\n- **Adversarial self-check**: all five findings are P2, so the tiered contract required evidence review only. Each cites a file:line and a concrete input; none was downgraded or called a false positive, and none was raised above P2. Two directions that looked like P1 candidates were ruled out with reproduction rather than confidence: the buffer overflow (reproduced `ENOBUFS` at the default cap and success at 512 MiB) and an arena fix closed without a build (T043 records the `ok:true` build).\n- **Operator review focus** (config.reviewFocus, verbatim): Review pass six. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-6.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file review/review-scope-6.txt, the diff command for each area, the recorded limits not to re-report and the holdout rule. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this lineage: the verdict is PASS and every open finding is an advisory that can be scheduled or fixed in place. It becomes required if any advisory is promoted after a new input shows a live failure, which the downgrade triggers below name.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC6-P2-001\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"title\": \"The per-run temp folder is removed on a clean exit only\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:16\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"findingClass\": \"instance-only\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC6-P2-002\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"title\": \"The suite isolation sets only the variable POSIX reads\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14\", \"dimension\": \"correctness\", \"findingClass\": \"instance-only\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC6-P2-003\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"title\": \"The isolation lever reaches one of the two suite configs\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14\", \"dimension\": \"traceability\", \"findingClass\": \"class-of-bug\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC6-P2-004\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"title\": \"The buffer regression test never asserts the premise it guards\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755\", \"dimension\": \"maintainability\", \"findingClass\": \"instance-only\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AC6-P2-005\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"title\": \"A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure\", \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:150\", \"dimension\": \"maintainability\", \"findingClass\": \"instance-only\"}\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Say in phase 035 which suite configs the per-run temp folder covers, or extend it to both.\",\n    \"State in phase 032 that an over-cap listing still reports as spawn_failed, or give it its own code.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Copy the eight-line TMPDIR block into vitest.stress.config.ts.\",\n    \"Assert the >1 MiB listing inside the 6,000-file regression test.\",\n    \"Branch on ENOBUFS in the builder's git() and throw listing_too_large.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"instance-only\", \"class-of-bug\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\"vitest.config.ts: per-run TMPDIR\", \"lib/metrics.ts durable root\", \"CI cancellation\", \"Windows runtime support\", \"vitest.stress.config.ts\", \"skill-advisor-stress workflow\", \"command-behaviour-guards arena builder block\", \"prepare-behaviour-arena git buffer\", \"regression coverage\", \"arena builder failure codes\", \"operator diagnosis\"],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Title | Dimension | File:line | Finding class | Disposition |\n|----|----------|-------|-----------|-----------|---------------|-------------|\n| AC6-P2-001 | P2 | The per-run temp folder is removed on a clean exit only | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:16` | instance-only | active, advisory |\n| AC6-P2-002 | P2 | The suite isolation sets only the variable POSIX reads | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14` | instance-only | active, advisory |\n| AC6-P2-003 | P2 | The isolation lever reaches one of the two suite configs | traceability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14` | class-of-bug | active, advisory |\n| AC6-P2-004 | P2 | The buffer regression test never asserts the premise it guards | maintainability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755` | instance-only | active, advisory |\n| AC6-P2-005 | P2 | A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure | maintainability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:150` | instance-only | active, advisory |\n\nEvidence and fix-completeness detail for each row is in the iteration narrative that raised it: `iterations/iteration-001.md` (AC6-P2-001, AC6-P2-002), `iteration-002.md` (AC6-P2-003) and `iteration-003.md` (AC6-P2-004, AC6-P2-005). The reducer owns `deep-review-findings-registry.json`; its `dimension` field falls back to the first reviewed dimension for every row, so the dimension column above follows the iteration that raised each finding instead.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\nP0: none.\n\nP1: none.\n\nP2 advisories, ordered by cost:\n\n1. **Cover the second suite config** (AC6-P2-003) — copy the TMPDIR block into `vitest.stress.config.ts`, or move it into a helper both configs import. This is the only advisory whose absence re-opens a closed phase's invariant.\n2. **Make the exit path complete or honest** (AC6-P2-001) — add `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` cleanup that re-raises, or state in the comment that a cancelled run leaves the folder.\n3. **Set the temp variables together** (AC6-P2-002) — assign `TMPDIR`, `TMP` and `TEMP` the way the spec-kit test setup already does.\n4. **Assert the test premise** (AC6-P2-004) — measure the listing and assert it passes 1 MiB before building.\n5. **Name the ceiling** (AC6-P2-005) — map `ENOBUFS` to a `listing_too_large` failure code.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- Phase 035: say the isolation covers `vitest.config.ts` only, or widen it to `vitest.stress.config.ts` and restate the handoff criterion as covering both suite entry points.\n- Phase 035: note that a signal-terminated run leaves its per-run folder, since the handoff criterion is about a completed run.\n- Phase 032: record that a listing above the raised cap still reports `spawn_failed`, so the next ceiling raise does not re-run the T043 investigation.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Task: copy the per-run temp block into `vitest.stress.config.ts`; verify with `rg -n \"TMPDIR\" runtime/vitest*.config.ts` returning both files and with one stress test asserting `os.tmpdir()` is inside a `sav-` folder.\n- Task: add a signal path to the temp cleanup; verify with a killed child process and a temp-folder listing.\n- Task: set `TMPDIR`, `TMP` and `TEMP` in the config; verify with `node -p \"require('os').tmpdir()\"` under each platform variable.\n- Task: assert the listing size in the 6,000-file test; verify the assertion fails when the loop count is halved.\n- Task: throw `listing_too_large` on `ENOBUFS`; verify with a stubbed `spawnSync` result carrying `error.code = 'ENOBUFS'`.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\nCore protocols:\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | Phase 035's REQ-001 and AC-001 name `vitest.config.ts` and a per-run temp folder, and `vitest.config.ts:14-15` does exactly that. Phase 032's T053 names a raised buffer in the builder's git helper, and `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:144-152` carries it. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | 035/T002 records the failing-then-passing run and \"0 sav- folders left after\"; AC-001 records `SUITE 2325 passed` with unchanged shared counts; AC-005 records the removed folder. 032/T053 records the failing first run and a 52-test pass; T043 records the `ok:true` arena build at `0173020dfc2` with 22 copied trees. |\n\nOverlay protocols: `playbook_capability` notApplicable (the playbook inspects the metrics folder after a manual hook run, which no suite config changes); `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime` and `feature_catalog_code` notApplicable (no skill, agent or catalog surface is in this area's diff).\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: **exempt**. The review target `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` carries no `acceptance-criteria.md` or `implementation-summary.md` at its root; the phase children that own checklists are outside this lineage's declared scope.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- Running the vitest suites or an arena build from this lineage: both write outside the lineage folder, so every claim was verified by reading the code, the recorded rows and a direct `spawnSync`/`mkdtemp` probe. A live suite run would add no evidence the reproduction does not already give for these two behaviours.\n- The Windows reach of `TMPDIR` (AC6-P2-002): out of the project's tested platforms (`rg -n \"win32\"` over the runtime returns nothing and no workflow runs on Windows).\n- The 512 MiB ceiling itself (AC6-P2-005): not reproducible here; the finding is about the diagnosis, not about a run above the cap.\n- Phase 032's T053 verify clause that accepts \"a refusal that is not `spawn_failed`\": not reported, because T043 records the stronger `ok:true` build.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Saturated directions: correctness, traceability, maintainability, plus a security read of the two boundaries the diff touches.\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\n- Selected review directions: the per-run temp folder and its exit path; the git buffer and its listing consumers; the regression test's premise; the failure code above the cap; the packet claims behind both changes.\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded; the loop stopped at `maxIterations=3` with no active P0 or P1.\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- `searchCoverage`: covered `resource_lifecycle`, `platform_env_variable`, `claim_scope_drift`, `test_premise_not_asserted`, `failure_code_diagnosis`; ruled out `input_size_overflow`, `socket_path_length`, `second_entry_point`, `checklist_evidence_gap`, `private_temp_mode`, `dotenv_copy_filter`; blocked `buffer_ceiling_reproduction`; deferred none.\n- `candidateCoverage`: 11 bug classes seen across three iterations; 5 carried findings, 5 ruled out, 1 blocked.\n- `searchDebt`: none (`searchDebtCount` 0 from the reducer). The blocked ceiling reproduction is a stated limit, not debt: no repository fixture can reach 512 MiB of paths.\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: unchanged listing truncation, socket-path overflow from a longer temp path, an arena fix closed without an arena build, a second suite entry point that already carries the lever, a private-mode regression, a dotenv leak through the larger read.\n- `cleanSearchProof`: `git()` throws on `result.error`, so an overflow cannot be read as a short listing; `mkdtempSync` creates mode `0700`; the copy filter is untouched by the diff.\n\n## Audit Appendix\n\n- **Convergence summary**: 3 iterations, stop reason `maxIterationsReached`; newFindingsRatio 1.0 → 0.3333 → 0.4; reducer convergenceScore 0.6; threshold 0.1 not reached, so the loop stopped at the configured ceiling rather than claiming convergence.\n- **Coverage summary**: configured dimensions covered per the reducer (`correctness`, `security`, `traceability`, `maintainability`); files reviewed 3 of 3 scope paths plus 5 integration surfaces.\n- **Ruled-out claims**: see the Search Ledger and `ruledOut` rows in `deltas/iter-001.jsonl`, `iter-002.jsonl` and `iter-003.jsonl`.\n- **Sources reviewed**: `review/review-brief-6.txt`, `review/review-scope-6.txt`, the three scope diffs, the three files at `85550ee946e`, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, `.skilled/bin/lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs`, both vitest configs, `runtime/package.json`, `.github/workflows/skill-advisor-stress.yml`, `035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/*`, `032-review-pass-five-remediation/{tasks.md,acceptance-criteria.md}`, and the `.opencode` mirror of both configs and the builder.\n- **Core Protocols**: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` pass.\n- **Overlay Protocols**: `playbook_capability` notApplicable, `skill_agent` notApplicable, `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable, `feature_catalog_code` notApplicable.\n- **Cross-reference integrity**: every `[SOURCE: …]` path in the three iteration narratives was read in this session; no path was inferred.\n- **Known limit**: the reducer's `dimension` field on the registry rows falls back to the first reviewed dimension; the report's registry table uses the true dimension per finding.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report — arena-config pass six\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict: PASS**\\n- **hasAdvisories: true** — five active P2 findings, no active P0 or P1.\\n- **P0/P1/P2 counts: 0 / 0 / 5** — the counts `review-verdict.cjs` derived from the lineage registry and state log, which are the counts this report uses.\\n- **Review scope**: the three paths `review/review-scope-6.txt` assigns to the `arena-config` area, diffed with the scope file's per-area command over `ddb12a6852c..85550ee946e`: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, `command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `vitest.config.ts` (62 insertions, 1 deletion).\\n- **Adversarial self-check**: all five findings are P2, so the tiered contract required evidence review only. Each cites a file:line and a concrete input; none was downgraded or called a false positive, and none was raised above P2. Two directions that looked like P1 candidates were ruled out with reproduction rather than confidence: the buffer overflow (reproduced `ENOBUFS` at the default cap and success at 512 MiB) and an arena fix closed without a build (T043 records the `ok:true` build).\\n- **Operator review focus** (config.reviewFocus, verbatim): Review pass six. First read specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-6.txt and follow it: it names your area by lineage label, the scope file review/review-scope-6.txt, the diff command for each area, the recorded limits not to re-report and the holdout rule. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this lineage: the verdict is PASS and every open finding is an advisory that can be scheduled or fixed in place. It becomes required if any advisory is promoted after a new input shows a live failure, which the downgrade triggers below name.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"AC6-P2-001\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"The per-run temp folder is removed on a clean exit only\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:16\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\", \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"instance-only\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"AC6-P2-002\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"The suite isolation sets only the variable POSIX reads\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\", \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"instance-only\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"AC6-P2-003\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"The isolation lever reaches one of the two suite configs\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"traceability\\\", \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"class-of-bug\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"AC6-P2-004\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"The buffer regression test never asserts the premise it guards\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"maintainability\\\", \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"instance-only\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"AC6-P2-005\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:150\\\", \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"maintainability\\\", \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"instance-only\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Say in phase 035 which suite configs the per-run temp folder covers, or extend it to both.\\\",\\n    \\\"State in phase 032 that an over-cap listing still reports as spawn_failed, or give it its own code.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Copy the eight-line TMPDIR block into vitest.stress.config.ts.\\\",\\n    \\\"Assert the >1 MiB listing inside the 6,000-file regression test.\\\",\\n    \\\"Branch on ENOBUFS in the builder's git() and throw listing_too_large.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"instance-only\\\", \\\"class-of-bug\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\\"vitest.config.ts: per-run TMPDIR\\\", \\\"lib/metrics.ts durable root\\\", \\\"CI cancellation\\\", \\\"Windows runtime support\\\", \\\"vitest.stress.config.ts\\\", \\\"skill-advisor-stress workflow\\\", \\\"command-behaviour-guards arena builder block\\\", \\\"prepare-behaviour-arena git buffer\\\", \\\"regression coverage\\\", \\\"arena builder failure codes\\\", \\\"operator diagnosis\\\"],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Title | Dimension | File:line | Finding class | Disposition |\\n|----|----------|-------|-----------|-----------|---------------|-------------|\\n| AC6-P2-001 | P2 | The per-run temp folder is removed on a clean exit only | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:16` | instance-only | active, advisory |\\n| AC6-P2-002 | P2 | The suite isolation sets only the variable POSIX reads | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14` | instance-only | active, advisory |\\n| AC6-P2-003 | P2 | The isolation lever reaches one of the two suite configs | traceability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14` | class-of-bug | active, advisory |\\n| AC6-P2-004 | P2 | The buffer regression test never asserts the premise it guards | maintainability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts:755` | instance-only | active, advisory |\\n| AC6-P2-005 | P2 | A listing above the cap is still reported as a spawn failure | maintainability | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:150` | instance-only | active, advisory |\\n\\nEvidence and fix-completeness detail for each row is in the iteration narrative that raised it: `iterations/iteration-001.md` (AC6-P2-001, AC6-P2-002), `iteration-002.md` (AC6-P2-003) and `iteration-003.md` (AC6-P2-004, AC6-P2-005). The reducer owns `deep-review-findings-registry.json`; its `dimension` field falls back to the first reviewed dimension for every row, so the dimension column above follows the iteration that raised each finding instead.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\nP0: none.\\n\\nP1: none.\\n\\nP2 advisories, ordered by cost:\\n\\n1. **Cover the second suite config** (AC6-P2-003) — copy the TMPDIR block into `vitest.stress.config.ts`, or move it into a helper both configs import. This is the only advisory whose absence re-opens a closed phase's invariant.\\n2. **Make the exit path complete or honest** (AC6-P2-001) — add `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` cleanup that re-raises, or state in the comment that a cancelled run leaves the folder.\\n3. **Set the temp variables together** (AC6-P2-002) — assign `TMPDIR`, `TMP` and `TEMP` the way the spec-kit test setup already does.\\n4. **Assert the test premise** (AC6-P2-004) — measure the listing and assert it passes 1 MiB before building.\\n5. **Name the ceiling** (AC6-P2-005) — map `ENOBUFS` to a `listing_too_large` failure code.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- Phase 035: say the isolation covers `vitest.config.ts` only, or widen it to `vitest.stress.config.ts` and restate the handoff criterion as covering both suite entry points.\\n- Phase 035: note that a signal-terminated run leaves its per-run folder, since the handoff criterion is about a completed run.\\n- Phase 032: record that a listing above the raised cap still reports `spawn_failed`, so the next ceiling raise does not re-run the T043 investigation.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Task: copy the per-run temp block into `vitest.stress.config.ts`; verify with `rg -n \\\"TMPDIR\\\" runtime/vitest*.config.ts` returning both files and with one stress test asserting `os.tmpdir()` is inside a `sav-` folder.\\n- Task: add a signal path to the temp cleanup; verify with a killed child process and a temp-folder listing.\\n- Task: set `TMPDIR`, `TMP` and `TEMP` in the config; verify with `node -p \\\"require('os').tmpdir()\\\"` under each platform variable.\\n- Task: assert the listing size in the 6,000-file test; verify the assertion fails when the loop count is halved.\\n- Task: throw `listing_too_large` on `ENOBUFS`; verify with a stubbed `spawnSync` result carrying `error.code = 'ENOBUFS'`.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\nCore protocols:\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | Phase 035's REQ-001 and AC-001 name `vitest.config.ts` and a per-run temp folder, and `vitest.config.ts:14-15` does exactly that. Phase 032's T053 names a raised buffer in the builder's git helper, and `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs:144-152` carries it. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | pass | 035/T002 records the failing-then-passing run and \\\"0 sav- folders left after\\\"; AC-001 records `SUITE 2325 passed` with unchanged shared counts; AC-005 records the removed folder. 032/T053 records the failing first run and a 52-test pass; T043 records the `ok:true` arena build at `0173020dfc2` with 22 copied trees. |\\n\\nOverlay protocols: `playbook_capability` notApplicable (the playbook inspects the metrics folder after a manual hook run, which no suite config changes); `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime` and `feature_catalog_code` notApplicable (no skill, agent or catalog surface is in this area's diff).\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: **exempt**. The review target `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` carries no `acceptance-criteria.md` or `implementation-summary.md` at its root; the phase children that own checklists are outside this lineage's declared scope.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- Running the vitest suites or an arena build from this lineage: both write outside the lineage folder, so every claim was verified by reading the code, the recorded rows and a direct `spawnSync`/`mkdtemp` probe. A live suite run would add no evidence the reproduction does not already give for these two behaviours.\\n- The Windows reach of `TMPDIR` (AC6-P2-002): out of the project's tested platforms (`rg -n \\\"win32\\\"` over the runtime returns nothing and no workflow runs on Windows).\\n- The 512 MiB ceiling itself (AC6-P2-005): not reproducible here; the finding is about the diagnosis, not about a run above the cap.\\n- Phase 032's T053 verify clause that accepts \\\"a refusal that is not `spawn_failed`\\\": not reported, because T043 records the stronger `ok:true` build.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Saturated directions: correctness, traceability, maintainability, plus a security read of the two boundaries the diff touches.\\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Selected review directions: the per-run temp folder and its exit path; the git buffer and its listing consumers; the regression test's premise; the failure code above the cap; the packet claims behind both changes.\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded; the loop stopped at `maxIterations=3` with no active P0 or P1.\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- `searchCoverage`: covered `resource_lifecycle`, `platform_env_variable`, `claim_scope_drift`, `test_premise_not_asserted`, `failure_code_diagnosis`; ruled out `input_size_overflow`, `socket_path_length`, `second_entry_point`, `checklist_evidence_gap`, `private_temp_mode`, `dotenv_copy_filter`; blocked `buffer_ceiling_reproduction`; deferred none.\\n- `candidateCoverage`: 11 bug classes seen across three iterations; 5 carried findings, 5 ruled out, 1 blocked.\\n- `searchDebt`: none (`searchDebtCount` 0 from the reducer). The blocked ceiling reproduction is a stated limit, not debt: no repository fixture can reach 512 MiB of paths.\\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: unchanged listing truncation, socket-path overflow from a longer temp path, an arena fix closed without an arena build, a second suite entry point that already carries the lever, a private-mode regression, a dotenv leak through the larger read.\\n- `cleanSearchProof`: `git()` throws on `result.error`, so an overflow cannot be read as a short listing; `mkdtempSync` creates mode `0700`; the copy filter is untouched by the diff.\\n\\n## Audit Appendix\\n\\n- **Convergence summary**: 3 iterations, stop reason `maxIterationsReached`; newFindingsRatio 1.0 → 0.3333 → 0.4; reducer convergenceScore 0.6; threshold 0.1 not reached, so the loop stopped at the configured ceiling rather than claiming convergence.\\n- **Coverage summary**: configured dimensions covered per the reducer (`correctness`, `security`, `traceability`, `maintainability`); files reviewed 3 of 3 scope paths plus 5 integration surfaces.\\n- **Ruled-out claims**: see the Search Ledger and `ruledOut` rows in `deltas/iter-001.jsonl`, `iter-002.jsonl` and `iter-003.jsonl`.\\n- **Sources reviewed**: `review/review-brief-6.txt`, `review/review-scope-6.txt`, the three scope diffs, the three files at `85550ee946e`, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, `.skilled/bin/lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs`, both vitest configs, `runtime/package.json`, `.github/workflows/skill-advisor-stress.yml`, `035-suite-metrics-and-start-shape/*`, `032-review-pass-five-remediation/{tasks.md,acceptance-criteria.md}`, and the `.opencode` mirror of both configs and the builder.\\n- **Core Protocols**: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` pass.\\n- **Overlay Protocols**: `playbook_capability` notApplicable, `skill_agent` notApplicable, `agent_cross_runtime` notApplicable, `feature_catalog_code` notApplicable.\\n- **Cross-reference integrity**: every `[SOURCE: …]` path in the three iteration narratives was read in this session; no path was inferred.\\n- **Known limit**: the reducer's `dimension` field on the registry rows falls back to the first reviewed dimension; the report's registry table uses the true dimension per finding.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/arena-config-6/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794817183197,"end":1794817215021}}}}
